       EVP_SIGNATURE-CMAC - The legacy EVP_PKEY MAC signature implementations

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The algorithms described here have legacy support for creating MACs
       using EEVVPP__DDiiggeessttSSiiggnnIInniitt(3) and related functions. This is not the
       preferred way of creating MACs. Instead you should use the newer
       EEVVPP__MMAACC__iinniitt(3) functions.  This mechanism is provided for backwards
       compatibility with older versions of OpenSSL.

       The same signature parameters can be set using
       EEVVPP__PPKKEEYY__CCTTXX__sseett__ppaarraammss(()) as can be set via EEVVPP__MMAACC__CCTTXX__sseett__ppaarraammss(())
       for the underlying EVP_MAC. See EEVVPP__MMAACC--HHMMAACC(7), EEVVPP__MMAACC--SSiipphhaasshh(7),
       EEVVPP__MMAACC--PPoollyy11330055(7) and EEVVPP__MMAACC--CCMMAACC(7) for details.

        See L<EVP_PKEY-HMAC(7)>, L<EVP_PKEY-Siphash(7)>, L<EVP_PKEY-Poly1305(7)> or
        L<EVP_PKEY-CMAC(7)> for details about parameters that are supported during the
        creation of an EVP_PKEY.

